# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
# Served from the deploy root, same as _redirects. Paths are matched top-down;
# `/admin/*` does NOT match `/admin` itself, so bare paths need their own rule.

# Keep the private screens out of the index.
#
# robots.txt used to Disallow these, which was the wrong tool and quietly the
# worse outcome: Disallow stops Google CRAWLING a URL, not indexing it. A
# disallowed page that is linked anywhere can still be listed URL-only, and
# because Google may not fetch it, it can never read a noindex and the entry
# cannot be removed. Serving `X-Robots-Tag: noindex` on a crawlable page is the
# instruction that actually takes effect. Nothing here is secret — these are
# login screens and an empty SPA shell; the real gate is Supabase Auth + RLS.
/admin
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/admin/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/login
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/account
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
